---
import RolePage from '../../components/pages/RolePage.astro';
---

<RolePage
  lang="en"
  title="For the sponsor committee — Rondo"
  description="Rondo for sponsor committees: organisations and personal sponsors, contacts, logos, digital passes and Club TV visibility."
  kicker="For your role"
  roleTitle="Sponsor committee"
  intro="Sponsors deserve the same care as members. In Rondo you manage organisations and personal sponsors, link contacts, issue digital passes and decide which sponsors appear on Club TV."
  demoLabel="Look at the demo"
  contactLabel="Contact us"
  contactHref="/en/contact/"
  screenshotSrc="/screenshot-sponsors-organisaties.jpg"
  screenshotAlt="Organisation sponsor overview with logo, sponsor role and Club TV status"
  screenshotWidth={1100}
  screenshotHeight={830}
  secondaryScreenshotSrc="/screenshot-sponsor-logo-club-tv.jpg"
  secondaryScreenshotAlt="Setting a sponsor logo and Club TV visibility"
  secondaryScreenshotWidth={615}
  secondaryScreenshotHeight={715}
  screenshotLayout="landscapePair"
  whatHeading="What this solves"
  bulletPoints={[
    'Manage organisations and personal sponsors as separate types, each with its own sponsor role and status.',
    'Link contacts to an organisation and decide which sponsor pass each contact can use.',
    'Rondo Sync can import organisations, contacts and protected logos from Sponsit without overwriting a manually added logo.',
    'An activated sponsor contact can only add or replace the logo of their own sponsor organisation in My details.',
    'Club TV only shows active sponsors with a logo set to Sometimes, Often or Always; Do not show keeps them off screen.',
    'Digital sponsor and Businessclub passes are available for Apple Wallet and Google Wallet.',
  ]}
  cards={[
    { title: 'One sponsor record', text: 'Organisations, personal sponsors and linked contacts stay together, without creating fake companies for personal sponsors.' },
    { title: 'Clear logo permissions', text: 'Administrators manage sponsor fields and imports; a sponsor contact can only update their own organisation’s logo.' },
    { title: 'Passes and Club TV', text: 'Issue the right Wallet pass and control how often each active sponsor logo appears on Club TV.' },
  ]}
  otherHeading="Other paths"
  otherPrefix="Also relevant:"
  otherAnd="and"
  otherLinks={[
    { href: '/en/for-gate-volunteer/', label: 'For access & events' },
    { href: '/en/for-communication/', label: 'For communication' },
  ]}
  hasExtra={true}
>
  <div class="sponsor-evidence role-container">
    <div class="sponsor-evidence-copy">
      <h2 class="gradient-text sponsor-evidence-heading">From sponsor record to safe visibility</h2>
      <p>
        An organisation can have several contacts; a personal sponsor remains one sponsor record linked to one person.
        Archiving a sponsor removes the sponsor-pass entitlement without deleting the person profile.
      </p>
      <p>
        Sponsor contacts can only replace their own organisation’s logo. Club TV then requires an active sponsor, a
        logo and a Sometimes, Often or Always setting. Rondo limits Always to six active sponsors with logos, keeping
        the rotation manageable.
      </p>
    </div>
    <figure class="sponsor-evidence-shot">
      <img
        class="zoomable-screenshot"
        src="/screenshot-sponsors-personen.jpg"
        alt="Personal sponsor overview with sponsor role, logo and Club TV status"
        width="1100"
        height="830"
        loading="lazy"
      />
    </figure>
  </div>
</RolePage>

<style>
  .sponsor-evidence {
    display: grid;
    gap: 1.5rem;
    max-width: 72rem;
    margin: 0 auto;
    align-items: center;
  }

  @media (min-width: 900px) {
    .sponsor-evidence { grid-template-columns: 0.9fr 1.1fr; }
  }

  .sponsor-evidence-heading {
    font-size: clamp(1.6rem, 2.6vw, 2.1rem);
    margin-bottom: 0.6rem;
  }

  .sponsor-evidence-copy p {
    color: #475569;
    line-height: 1.7;
    margin: 0.75rem 0 0;
  }

  .sponsor-evidence-shot {
    border: 1px solid #D8E3EE;
    border-radius: 1rem;
    overflow: hidden;
    background: #FFFFFF;
    box-shadow: 0 18px 45px rgba(0, 27, 96, 0.16);
  }

  .sponsor-evidence-shot img {
    width: 100%;
    height: auto;
    display: block;
  }
</style>
